60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option A is a recipe for resentment. The person in the cold room will either suffer in silence or be the villain who raises the bill for everyone.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the easiest to manage! No fancy templates, no year-end nightmares, just one division and we're done! I love it!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is simple, but it ignores the reality of our different usage patterns. I worry it will leave the same rumors of unfairness as before.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is far too expensive and disruptive. Option A, while simple, offers no protection against the winter spikes I've seen in the statements.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A seems like it would be the most peaceful because it's the simplest, but I'm worried it might make some people feel it's not fair.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, simplicity is a luxury that often comes at the cost of someone else's comfort. I find Option B far more sophisticated and equitable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, ""sophisticated"" usually means ""takes a long time to do!"" Option B means someone has to track everything for a whole year and then do a giant calculation!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Option B provides a level of predictability that could soothe the tension. It allows us to plan our finances without the monthly stress of fluctuating bills.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Option B is the most rational choice. It smooths out the seasonal peaks, preventing the ""second rent"" effect in winter, without the cost of sub-meters.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"If Option B helps people not worry about the money every month, then maybe that will stop the fighting? I like that idea.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Minato. It removes the immediate psychological pressure of the winter bill, preventing anyone from having to wear a coat indoors to save a few coins.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,But who does the year-end settle?! I've seen how that goes! It's a total disaster and takes hours of arguing over who used what!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,We can use a simple template for the year-end settle. The peace of mind throughout the year is worth a few hours of work in December.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. The stability of a fixed seasonal rate is far more valuable than the convenience of a flat split. It allows for actual budgeting.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think if we all agree to be kind during the year-end settle, it will be okay. I'll help with the math if it makes people happy!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems the weight of logic and stability is tipping the scales. I believe Option B is the only choice that respects both the wallet and the thermometer.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I still hate the idea of a big year-end chore, but if everyone else is okay with it and Minato is helping... I guess I can live with it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am satisfied with Option B. It addresses the unfairness of the current system while providing a calm, predictable environment for us all.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I am in agreement. Option B solves the volatility issue and avoids the prohibitive cost of Option C. It is the most sustainable path forward.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy if everyone is happy. Let's go with the one that keeps us all friends.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
